===Noun===
{{fr-noun|f|mesdemoiselles}}

# [[Miss]] (as a form of address)

===Noun===
{{fr-noun|f|demoiselles}}

# [[Miss]] (as a title with a name)

====Usage notes====
* Not used for an older woman unless she is clearly unmarried.
* As of February 21, 2012, the use of the word ''mademoiselle'' is prohibited from use in official forms and registries in France.<ref>{{cite-journal|en|author=Scott Sayare|title=‘Mademoiselle’ Exits Official France|work=The New York Times|date=2012-02-22|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2012/02/23/world/europe/france-drops-mademoiselle-from-official-use.html|issn=0362-4331}}</ref><ref>{{cite-web|en|title=Mademoiselle is no longer an official French woman|work=Reuters|date=2012-02-23|url=https://www.reuters.com/article/us-france-mademoiselle-idUSTRE81M1DR20120223}}</ref>
* The form {{m|fr|madelle}} (a {{glossary|blend}} of {{m|fr|madame}} and ''mademoiselle'') has been suggested as a replacement, but never caught on.

